From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:28:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/38] feat(asr): add SessionLaneManager (lane allocator) for
 N>1 ASR worker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The native N>1 ASR voice worker (qwen3_asr_worker.cpp) includes
runtime/asrStreamingSessionRuntime.h for rt::SessionLaneManager +
rt::LaneOwnerKind — static-partition lane reservation over the shared
HybridCacheManager batch rows. The worker runs the vanilla one-shot
LLMInferenceRuntime path and uses the lane manager for reservation only.

This header/source did not exist on the Base TTS N>1 port branch (it was
only ever introduced by the deferred ASR-streaming spike v080-0002/0005),
so the full v0.8.0 stack could not be built from this single branch.

Add a MINIMAL header+source containing ONLY SessionLaneManager and
LaneOwnerKind. The full chunked-streaming wrapper (AsrStreamingSessionRuntime
with appendChunk/beginAsrSession + per-lane KV reset + LLMInferenceRuntime
hooks) is intentionally NOT included, so this does not drag the deferred
streaming spike (or any talker-prefill changes) into the Base build.

The .cpp is picked up automatically by the existing
file(GLOB_RECURSE RUNTIME_CPP_SRCS "runtime/*.cpp") into edgellmCore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

